 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items?limit=<integer>&cursor=<opaque>` →
+  `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": <string|null>}`: items ordered by `id`.
+  `limit` is optional (default `20`, range `1`–`100`). Omit `cursor` on the
+  first request; pass `next_cursor` unchanged to fetch the next page. The final
+  page has `next_cursor: null`. Invalid limits or cursors return HTTP 400 with
+  `{"error": "..."}`.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
